# Copy to /var/lib/leandro/secrets.env inside the VM, chmod 600 leandro:users.
# Phase 1 needs none of these to boot; phase 2 fills them in.

# Claude Code subscription OAuth token (generate: `claude setup-token` on your PC)
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=example-paste-token-here

# Phase 2 (Google Chat via Pub/Sub — values from scripts/setup-gchat.sh output)
GOOGLE_CHAT_PROJECT_ID=example-project-id
GOOGLE_CHAT_SUBSCRIPTION_NAME=projects/example-project-id/subscriptions/hermes-chat-events-sub
GOOGLE_CHAT_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=/var/lib/leandro/gchat-sa.json
GOOGLE_CHAT_ALLOWED_USERS=you@example.com
# DM space id — target for watcher diagnoses via `hermes send` (find it with:
# `hermes send --list google_chat` once you have DM'd the app at least once)
GOOGLE_CHAT_HOME_CHANNEL=spaces/EXAMPLE

# Phase 3 (watcher, optional): Google Chat *incoming webhook* URL — a space
# webhook, unrelated to the Pub/Sub app above. Alerts and the facts-only
# fallback are posted there when a diagnosis fails. Unset = incident reports
# only land in /var/lib/leandro/incidents.
# LEANDRO_WEBHOOK_URL=

# Watcher token accounting: one JSONL line per `hermes -z` run (incident
# count, duration, --usage-file token usage). Default shown; uncomment only
# to override. Empty value = off. See README.md for the runs/day + jq recipes.
# LEANDRO_RUNS_LOG=/var/lib/leandro/runs.jsonl

# Watcher "blind" alert out-of-band channel: a full ntfy topic URL (not just
# a topic name — e.g. https://ntfy.sh/<topic>), POSTed to directly by the
# watcher (watcher/leandro_watcher.py:_ping_blind), independent of the ntfy
# gateway platform below. Fires when the API-server watch stream has been
# unreachable past LEANDRO_BLIND_AFTER_SECONDS — the point is a channel that
# survives the VM's own network (or Google Chat) being what's down. Unset =
# blind alerts only go to LEANDRO_WEBHOOK_URL / LEANDRO_CHAT_TARGET.
# LEANDRO_NTFY_URL=https://ntfy.sh/example-topic

# ntfy gateway platform: DISABLED in hermes/config.yaml (see the comment
# there) — the topic name is the ONLY auth on the inbound side, so on public
# ntfy.sh anyone who learns it can talk to Leandro and read his replies.
# If you ever enable it: treat NTFY_TOPIC as a SECRET (high entropy, never
# a guessable word) and prefer a self-hosted server with NTFY_TOKEN/ACLs.
# NOTE: bare topic NAME, not a URL, unlike LEANDRO_NTFY_URL above.
# NTFY_TOPIC=
# NTFY_SERVER_URL=https://ntfy.sh
# NTFY_TOKEN=
# NTFY_HOME_CHANNEL=

# webhook gateway platform: NOT wired (see the commented block in
# hermes/config.yaml — its HMAC secret has no env-var indirection in
# gateway/platforms/webhook.py, so it can't be safely sourced from this file
# without also hand-editing the git-tracked config.yaml). Listed here only
# because the watcher already has the client side implemented and documented
# in README.md (experimental — falls back to the `hermes -z` subprocess path
# on any failure):
# LEANDRO_GATEWAY_WEBHOOK_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8644/webhooks/leandro-watcher
# LEANDRO_GATEWAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
